---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Layout title="Store Policy — Saturday Boring Cereal">
  <PageHeader
    kicker="Terms and conditions apply"
    title="Store "
    accent="Policy"
    lede="The methodology, posted by the register where nobody reads it. Every rule below is actually followed, which is the least advertising-like thing on this website."
  />

  <div class="policy wrap">
    <section>
      <h2>§1 — The Taste Scale</h2>
      <p>
        Every cereal is scored 0–10, decimals allowed. The scale is inherited from years of
        careful record-keeping and will not be changed, recalibrated, or explained. An 8.5 is a
        very good morning. Nothing has earned a 10. Nothing may ever earn a 10.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>§2 — The Numbers</h2>
      <p>
        Nutrition is transcribed from the physical box and cross-checked against USDA FoodData
        Central where possible. The label lists values per serving, and every box states a different
        serving, so this store scales them all to 100 grams before showing or grading them. The
        label's serving size is still noted on each box's page. When a label doesn't state a value
        — protein %DV, poly/mono fats — this store prints <em>“not listed”</em>
        rather than inventing a number. The FDA only requires protein %DV when a protein claim is
        made; most boxes stay quiet, and so do we.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>§3 — What Gets Shelved</h2>
      <p>
        Granolas and healthier cereals, weighted toward things a functioning adult eats on
        purpose: flakes, clusters, high-fiber, high-protein. Neon marshmallow products are outside
        the jurisdiction of this regulatory body.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>§4 — On Clusters</h2>
      <p>
        Flakes are only acceptable when accompanied by clusters. This is store policy. Complaints
        may be filed with the spoon.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>§5 — Returns</h2>
      <p>All opinions are final. No refunds. Total regret: 0.00.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="overall">
      <h2>§6 — The Tier</h2>
      <p>
        The Taste score answers one question: is it good. The <em>Tier</em> answers a nosier one —
        is it good <em>for you</em>, too. It is half the spoon's verdict and half the box's own
        numbers, weighed per 100 grams so a box can't win by declaring a bigger bowl. The spoon's
        half is squared before it counts, so a 9 keeps 81 points, a 7 keeps 49, and a 3 keeps 9.
        A cereal that tastes bad stays bad no matter how many vitamins it brags about: even a
        perfect label can't lift a 3 into the top tiers. On the numbers side, protein counts most
        (40%), then low total sugar (30%), then fiber (20%), then low saturated fat (10%); only
        the figures printed on the label are admitted as evidence. Protein is judged by its % Daily
        Value, which the label adjusts for protein quality: 35% per 100 grams earns full marks.
        When a box prints only grams, we assume 1.25% DV per gram and say so. Full marks for fiber
        is 12 grams; 20 grams of sugar or 8 grams of saturated fat scores zero. A cereal that
        tastes like a birthday but eats like dessert lands mid-pack, and a virtuous brick nobody
        enjoys does no better. Tiers run <em>S, A, B, C, D, F</em>, handed out like a strict
        lunchroom. S is a blue ribbon pinned on the single best box on the shelf — held by exactly
        one at a time, and taken away the moment something outscores it; an A is already a very good
        morning. Unrated boxes get no tier, because we will not invent a taste we never had. The
        formula lives in the code, not on this poster; change a target and every box on the shelf is
        re-ranked at once.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>

  .policy {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-top: 34px;
    background: #fffdf4;
    border: 1px solid #e0d5b8;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
    padding: 30px 34px;
      margin-bottom: 70px;
  }

  section + section {
    margin-top: 22px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cherry);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  p {
    font-family: var(--fine);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #3d2c15;
  }
</style>
